TERMS OF USE

This repository holds the companion datasets, code and documentation for
"Modern Biostatistics for the Health Sciences, Volume I: Health Research Methods
and Study Design" and "Biostatistics with R & AI, Volume II: An Interactive Guide
to Data Analysis" by Lida Gharibvand.

All of it is original work. The HALO datasets are simulated. They were designed
and generated by the author and are not derived from, extracted from, or based on
any real patient record, registry, trial or other existing dataset. The generating
code, the documentation, the data dictionary and the analysis scripts are likewise
the author's own work.

WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING

Permission is granted, free of charge, to any person or institution to use,
download, copy and adapt the contents of this repository for the following
purposes:

  1. Learning. Working through the books, running the code, completing the
     exercises, and using the data for your own study or practice.

  2. Teaching. Using the datasets, the code and the documentation in a course,
     workshop, seminar or training session, including making copies for enrolled
     students, whether or not the course charges tuition.

  3. Scholarship. Using the datasets in academic research, methodological work,
     or published articles, including worked illustrations of statistical
     methods.

In each case, please credit the source as set out in CITATION.cff.

WHAT REQUIRES WRITTEN PERMISSION

All other rights are reserved. In particular, the following require the prior
written permission of the author:

  1. Including these materials, in whole or in substantial part, in a textbook,
     course pack sold commercially, training product, software product or other
     work offered for sale or licence.

  2. Redistributing the datasets or the code as a dataset collection, package or
     repository of your own, whether modified or unmodified.

  3. Using these materials to train, fine-tune, evaluate or benchmark a machine
     learning model or an artificial intelligence system offered commercially.

  4. Any use that presents the materials as your own work, or that removes or
     obscures the attribution.

Requests for permission are welcome and are usually granted for academic
purposes. Please write to the author.

NO WARRANTY

The HALO datasets are simulated and are provided for teaching and learning only.
No participant, clinic, ward, physician or treatment in them is real. Nothing in
them is evidence about any real treatment, and no figure computed from them
describes any real population. The materials are provided "as is", without
warranty of any kind, express or implied, and the author accepts no liability for
any claim, damage or other consequence arising from their use.

THIS IS NOT AN OPEN-SOURCE LICENCE

These terms are deliberately narrower than an open-source or Creative Commons
licence. They are intended to let teachers teach and students learn freely, while
reserving the author's commercial rights in material that is also published in
print. Broader terms may be issued in future; nothing here prevents the author
from granting them.

